@startuml Add Class Schedule by Admin
actor Admin
participant ": ClassManagementPage " as ClassManagementPage
participant ": ClassScheduleEditor " as ClassScheduleEditor
participant ": Router " as Router
participant ": ClassGroupController " as ClassGroupController
participant ": ClassGroupService " as ClassGroupService
participant ": ClassGroupRepository " as ClassGroupRepository
database Database

Admin->ClassManagementPage: 1. Admin clicks to Edit Class
    activate Admin
    activate ClassManagementPage

ClassManagementPage->ClassScheduleEditor: 2. Open Edit Modal with ClassScheduleEditor
    activate ClassScheduleEditor
    deactivate ClassManagementPage

Admin->ClassScheduleEditor: 3. Add Schedule (select days, time, period)

ClassScheduleEditor->ClassScheduleEditor: 4. Validate Schedule Data

ClassScheduleEditor->ClassManagementPage: 5. Update schedules in form state
    activate ClassManagementPage
    deactivate ClassScheduleEditor

Admin->ClassManagementPage: 6. Click "Cập nhật" button

ClassManagementPage->Router: 7. Send PUT /api/classgroup/{id} with schedules
    deactivate ClassManagementPage
    activate Router

Router->ClassGroupController: 8. Route Request to Controller
    deactivate Router
    activate ClassGroupController

ClassGroupController->ClassGroupService: 9. UpdateAsync(dto)
    deactivate ClassGroupController
    activate ClassGroupService

ClassGroupService->ClassGroupRepository: 10. GetByIdAsync(classGroupId)
    activate ClassGroupRepository
    ClassGroupRepository->Database: 11. Query ClassGroup by Id
    activate Database
    Database-->ClassGroupRepository: 12. Return ClassGroup
    deactivate Database
    ClassGroupRepository-->ClassGroupService: 13. Return ClassGroup entity
    deactivate ClassGroupRepository

ClassGroupService->ClassGroupService: 14. Update ClassGroup fields and schedules

ClassGroupService->ClassGroupRepository: 15. UpdateAsync(classGroup)
    activate ClassGroupRepository

ClassGroupRepository->Database: 16. UPDATE ClassGroup and Schedules
    activate Database

Database-->ClassGroupRepository: 17. ClassGroup Updated Successfully
    deactivate Database

ClassGroupRepository-->ClassGroupService: 18. ClassGroup Updated
    deactivate ClassGroupRepository

ClassGroupService->ClassGroupService: 19. Map to ClassGroupDto

ClassGroupService-->ClassGroupController: 20. Return ClassGroupDto
    deactivate ClassGroupService
    activate ClassGroupController

ClassGroupController-->Router: 21. Send Success Response
    activate Router
    deactivate ClassGroupController

Router-->ClassManagementPage: 22. Class Schedule Added Successfully
    activate ClassManagementPage
    deactivate Router

ClassManagementPage->ClassManagementPage: 23. Show Success Message and Close Modal

ClassManagementPage-->Admin: 24. Show Updated Class with Schedule
    deactivate ClassManagementPage
    deactivate Admin
@enduml





